Why Is Demand Increasing
5G and broadband expansion: Faster connections and improvements in network latency are helping make streamed gaming more practical across smartphones, computers, and connected televisions.
Hardware-independent gaming: Cloud platforms allow players to access demanding games without purchasing high-end local gaming hardware.
Subscription-based services: Gaming subscriptions and platform ecosystems are creating new distribution models and recurring revenue opportunities for service providers.

Cloud Gaming Market Watch: AI-Powered Streaming and Cross-Platform Access
Cloud gaming providers are investing in AI-assisted resource allocation, improved video encoding, and infrastructure optimization to deliver more consistent gameplay. Expansion across mobile devices, smart televisions, and other connected platforms is also broadening the potential user base, while service providers continue to address latency, bandwidth, and licensing challenges.

