Why This Market Matters
Cloud gaming is changing how games are distributed and accessed by shifting much of the processing workload from local devices to remote infrastructure. The model can reduce hardware barriers for consumers and create new opportunities for game publishers, telecom operators, and cloud providers, although network quality, operating costs, and content rights remain important commercial factors.

